{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Peter Prepares for Final Exams"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The Registrar's Office"}, {"type": "position", "content": 1}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 10}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Accurately use information about people's jobs and places of work in communicative situations"}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le10ob01re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The First Conditional"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use the First Conditional to talk about actions and situations in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are two parts to the sentence.  One part is the <span class=\"strong\">condition</span>. The other part is the <span class=\"strong\">result</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Form:<br> <span class=\"italic\">If + subject + Simple Present tense  + subject + will </span><br> You use a comma after the condition in this form. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can change the two parts of the sentence so that the result comes first."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Condition\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Result\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If I stay at the company,</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'll gain a lot of valuable experience in my field.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Result\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Condition\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I won't be able to work at MechaTech</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">if I start the courses.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Making and Responding to Promises"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Future tense (with <span class=\"italic\">will</span>) to make promises."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can start the sentence with \u201cI promise I'll \u2026 \u201d or \u201cI promise to \u2026 \u201d. "}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can respond to promises with an expression like:  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span  class=\"italic\">Great, thank you!<br> Alright.<br> OK. <br>That's fine.<br> Sure, that works.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">John</span>: I will help you with your math homework tomorrow.<br><span class=\"strong\">Helen</span>:  Great, thank you!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:  I promise I'll take the courses this summer. <br><span class=\"strong\">Registrar</span>:  Alright."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "co-op program "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "A program of study combined with work experiences. Co-op is short for co-operative."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I'm in the co-op program in the Business department.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le10ob01aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about programs of study."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "accounting "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "professional activity of keeping financial records "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm enrolled in an accounting course next term."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le10ob01aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "human resources "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "department of a company responsible for hiring employees, also called HR "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I have an HR course starting next week."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le10ob01aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "math"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "short form of mathematics, the study of the calculation of numbers"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Math is important for accounting."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le10ob01aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "Registrar"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the person or office responsible for enrolling students in an educational institution "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  You have to apply to the Registrar for special permission."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le10ob01aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "obligatory "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "describes something you have to do "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Those courses are obligatory for your degree. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le10ob01aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to enroll"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to sign up; to be registered to take a course"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: I enrolled in three courses this term."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le10ob01aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "course "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a series of lessons about a certain topic "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I enrolled in four courses next term."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le10ob01aud08"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write a list of 6 hypothetical situations on separate pieces of paper. Use the Present tense, like <span class=\"italic\">I take a co-op program</span> or <span class=\"italic\">I study accounting</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Ask a partner to write another 6 situations."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Combine the papers."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Take one paper. Complete a sentence using the situation on the paper. Use the <span class=\"italic\">\u201cIf ... + I will ...\u201d</span> structure, like <span class=\"italic\">If I take a co-op program, I will work in a large company</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Explain why."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Your partner takes a paper and completes a sentence."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Continue taking turns."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write 6 situations."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I practice making hypothetical statements."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I discuss why."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn5le10ob01re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn5le10ob01re2img05.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn5le10ob01re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:  Hello. I'm working as an intern at a software company right now.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Registrar</span>: Oh yes, that's the co-op program in the Business department.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn5le10ob01re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Yes. I would like to continue working there. If I stay at the company, I'll gain a lot of valuable experience in my field.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Registrar</span>: OK.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: I enrolled in one math, two accounting and one HR course starting next week. I won't be able to work at MechaTech if I start the courses.", "id": 2, "time": "8000", "image": "engenn5le10ob01re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Registrar</span>: Those courses are obligatory for your degree. Maybe you could study part-time.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Do you mean take fewer courses?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Registrar</span>:  Yes. You have to apply to the Registrar for special permission. If you take two courses now, you will take other courses during the summer.", "id": 3, "time": "25000", "image": "engenn5le10ob01re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:  Great!  I promise I'll take the courses this summer. Thank you!<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Registrar</span>: Alright, here's the application form.", "id": 4, "time": "43000", "image": "engenn5le10ob01re2img05.jpg"}]}}]}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about subjects to study."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "  I can talk about hypothetical actions and events in the future. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can make and respond to promises."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " When do you make promises? "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What promises do you make?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": 